descriptions:
The Promoting HIV Self-testing for Young Men in Kenya project aims to close the HIV testing gap among men in Kenya by promoting HIV Self-Testing (HIVST).  Its objectives are:
• To innovate service delivery models linking public and private sectors through design of HIVST promotion tools targeting young people; 
• To increase uptake of HIVST through awareness raising on self-testing services for at-risk men ages 20-34;
• To create a sustainable supply of HIVST kits that are conveniently available and accessible for men in need of HIVST; and 
• To create an enabling environment for HIVST scale up and sustainability by adapting and running the intervention through existing health system and structures.
